# Agents

This app's agents, one directory each, named for the agent: `assistant/` holds `agent.md` (who the agent is
and how it uses the app's tools) and `host.yaml` (embedded in {{ .inputs.repo_name }}, for the life of the app).
The layout is Nanite's convention for embedding hosts (docs/embedding.md in github.com/hollis-labs/nanite).

**Nothing in the app opens these files yet.** They are the standard starting point; the agent becomes live
when the app is wired to open it with Nanite. Until then, editing them changes nothing at run time.

Check them with Nanite: `nanite validate agents/assistant`, or `nanite -C agents/assistant` to talk to the
agent from a terminal. Run-time state belongs under the app's own data directory, not here.

`agents.dir: agents/` is resolved through Substrate's `agents.Resolve` after operator config merges.
With `SUBSTRATE_CONFIG`, relative paths are beside that file; with embedded config, they are beside
`substrate.yaml` in the working directory (the generated checkout's root). For an installed app, set an
absolute `agents.dir` or install `agents/` beside the operator config. Paths are published as
`agent-directory.layout`; runtime data resolves to `$XDG_STATE_HOME/{{ .inputs.repo_name }}/agents/<name>`
(default `~/.local/state/{{ .inputs.repo_name }}/agents/<name>`). Resolution creates no directories.
